menu "WFH"
    config WFH_DUMP_FRAMEBUFFER
        bool "Dump the framebuffer over serial at boot"
        default n
        help
            Snapshots what LVGL rendered and prints it as base64, for
            tools/grab-screen.sh to turn back into a PNG. A display can be
            wrong in two places — LVGL drew it wrong, or the panel received
            it wrong — and from outside the board those look identical.
            Off by default: it costs 2.5s of boot and a lot of serial.
endmenu
